PR #517 "courses: expert level, ratings can be empty" - diff of the generated openapi.json, response of GET /v1/courses/{slug}:
   "level": {
     "type": "string",
-    "enum": ["beginner", "intermediate", "advanced"]
+    "enum": ["beginner", "intermediate", "advanced", "expert"]
   },
   "averageRating": {
-    "type": "number"
+    "type": ["number", "null"]
   },
+  "badges": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },

Android 3.9 model (Kotlin, kotlinx.serialization):
enum class Level { @SerialName("beginner") BEGINNER, @SerialName("intermediate") INTERMEDIATE, @SerialName("advanced") ADVANCED }
data class CourseDto(..., val level: Level, val averageRating: Double, ...), decoded with Json { ignoreUnknownKeys = true }

Reviewer's comment: "Only additions, nothing removed - safe to merge."

Statement: "Adding \"expert\" to the level enum is safe for the Android app, because a value was added and none was removed."

